    "body": "This post outlines a hypothetical framework for prompt regression testing when evaluating changes to prompts for local language models. The core idea is to establish a consistent method for assessing if new prompt versions negatively impact model performance on existing tasks. We propose using a fixed set of 12 test prompts [F1] to ensure comparability. These prompts should cover a range of scenarios, including those with sufficient information for a clear answer and those where the provided information is insufficient [F3]. The evaluation process involves running both the old and new prompt versions against the same model configuration and settings [F2]. This direct comparison is crucial for isolating the effect of the prompt change itself. It's important to note that this is a hypothetical experiment, and no actual improvement results are available at this stage [F4]. The goal is to set up a repeatable process for future analysis.",
